<hr>
<p dir="auto">Similar to above, I've also noticed a similar pattern with different numbers when I change the values that I'm filtering by. Specifically, I changed <code class="notranslate">category='AssetType'</code> and <code class="notranslate">name='TV Ad'</code> (stats on these below).<br>
When I change it to these values that are more frequently occuring in the <em>tag</em> table than the ones shown above, I see the exact same pattern, but with <code class="notranslate">LIMIT 20</code> and <code class="notranslate">LIMIT 10</code>, where limiting to 10 results uses the vector index whereas 20 does not.</p>
<p dir="auto">This pattern makes me think if perhaps it's a memory issue?<br>
My <code class="notranslate">shared_buffers</code> is currently set to '4GB', which is 25% of the memory on the machine.</p>
<p dir="auto">My tables are not extremely large. Here are some stats that might be relevant:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><em>tag</em> table size: 22,233</li>
<li><em>taggeditem</em> table size: 81,176,748</li>
<li><em>segment</em> table size: 3,969,216</li>
<li>no. of _taggeditem_s for (<code class="notranslate">category</code>='Cinematography' + <code class="notranslate">name</code>='Wide Framing') = 413,482</li>
<li>no. of _taggeditem_s for (<code class="notranslate">category</code>='AssetType' + <code class="notranslate">name</code>='TV Ad') = 3,124,493</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Is this kind of behavior expected? I expect the tables to grow to billions of rows, and would appreciate any insight into how to mitigate this and make the same query consistently use the index regardless of the values one's filtering by.</p></div></div><div class="IssueBodyTaskList__-FlQre"><!--$!--><template></template><button data-component="IconButton" type="button" class="prc-Button-ButtonBase-9n-Xk ReactionViewerAnchorButton__BIXMSn prc-Button-IconButton-fyge7" data-inactive="true" data-loading="false" data-no-visuals="true" data-size="small" data-variant="default" aria-labelledby="_R_1al4utkp85_"><svg data-component="Octicon" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" class="octicon octicon-smiley" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" display="inline-block" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:text-bottom"><path d="M8 0a8 8 0 1 1 0 16A8 8 0 0 1 8 0ZM1.5 8a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 13 0 6.5 6.5 0 0 0-13 0Zm3.82 1.636a.75.75 0 0 1 1.038.175l.007.009c.103.118.22.222.35.31.264.178.683.37 1.285.37.602 0 1.02-.192 1.285-.371.13-.088.247-.192.35-.31l.007-.008a.75.75 0 0 1 1.222.87l-.022-.015c.02.013.021.015.021.015v.001l-.001.002-.002.003-.005.007-.014.019a2.066 2.066 0 0 1-.184.213c-.16.166-.338.316-.53.445-.63.418-1.37.638-2.127.629-.946 0-1.652-.308-2.126-.63a3.331 3.331 0 0 1-.715-.657l-.014-.02-.005-.006-.002-.003v-.002h-.001l.613-.432-.614.43a.75.75 0 0 1 .183-1.044ZM12 7a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0ZM5 8a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Zm5.25 2.25.592.416a97.71 97.71 0 0 0-.592-.416Z"></path></svg></button><span class="prc-TooltipV2-Tooltip-tLeuB" data-direction="n" data-component="Tooltip" aria-hidden="true" id="_R_1al4utkp85_">Reactions are currently unavailable</span><!--/$--></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><!--$--><div data-testid="issue-viewer-comments-container" class="react-comments-container"><div class="commentsContainer__BJKxiK"><div><h2 class="sr-only" id="_R_1eutkp85_">Activity</h2><ol id="issue-timeline" data-testid=